272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (K-Nearest Neighbors \(KNN\) is used in hand gesture recognition to classify gestures based on their similarity to nearby data points. It works by identifying the k nearest neighbors \(data points with similar features\) to a given hand gesture image and assigning the majority class among these neighbors as the predicted class for the input image. KNN is effective for hand gesture recognition as it relies on the idea that similar gestures are likely to belong to the same class.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
